WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.369
Every single day,

2
00:00:01.369 --> 00:00:05.023
engineers lose sleep debugging production servers at three

3
00:00:05.023 --> 00:00:05.936
AM Why?

4
00:00:05.936 --> 00:00:09.589
Because existing AI models live trapped inside browser

5
00:00:09.589 --> 00:00:10.046
tabs,

6
00:00:10.046 --> 00:00:13.699
completely blind to the operating systems where code

7
00:00:13.699 --> 00:00:14.613
actually runs.

8
00:00:14.613 --> 00:00:17.690
Now you might wonder: why not just hand

9
00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:19.997
an AI agent root shell access?

10
00:00:19.997 --> 00:00:23.074
Because that is like handing a toddler a

11
00:00:23.074 --> 00:00:23.459
flamethrower.

12
00:00:23.459 --> 00:00:26.536
One prompt injection or hallucinated command can delete

13
00:00:26.536 --> 00:00:28.074
your entire production database.

14
00:00:28.074 --> 00:00:30.689
That is why we built ARGUS.

15
00:00:30.689 --> 00:00:34.175
Engineered in memory-safe Rust across fourteen sovereign crates

16
00:00:34.175 --> 00:00:37.662
by R Jan Steve Daniel for the Nebius

17
00:00:37.662 --> 00:00:39.841
and NVIDIA Global AI Hackathon.

18
00:00:39.841 --> 00:00:43.327
A zero-trust autonomous daemon running directly on Linux.

19
00:00:43.327 --> 00:00:45.747
Security is not an afterthought;

20
00:00:45.747 --> 00:00:47.683
it is our foundation.

21
00:00:47.683 --> 00:00:51.555
ARGUS cages every tool execution inside Landlock Linux

22
00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:52.523
Security Modules,

23
00:00:52.523 --> 00:00:54.459
cgroups v2 resource ceilings,

24
00:00:54.459 --> 00:00:55.911
and unprivileged namespaces.

25
00:00:55.911 --> 00:00:58.330
Even if an agent hallucinates,

26
00:00:58.330 --> 00:01:00.266
the kernel forbids escapes.

27
00:01:00.266 --> 00:01:03.631
When a port collision freezes your web service,

28
00:01:03.631 --> 00:01:06.575
ARGUS detects the failure through eBPF telemetry,

29
00:01:06.575 --> 00:01:08.257
investigates the rogue PID,

30
00:01:08.257 --> 00:01:10.780
executes safe remediation in two seconds,

31
00:01:10.780 --> 00:01:14.145
and dispatches a cellular voice call to the

32
00:01:14.145 --> 00:01:14.986
lead engineer.

33
00:01:14.986 --> 00:01:17.915
This is what computing should look like.

34
00:01:17.915 --> 00:01:21.262
An operating system where AI is not an

35
00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.099
intrusive sidebar,

36
00:01:22.099 --> 00:01:23.354
but a reliable,

37
00:01:23.354 --> 00:01:24.610
sovereign kernel guardian.

38
00:01:24.610 --> 00:01:25.865
Welcome to ARGUS.

39
00:01:25.865 --> 00:01:26.283
Autonomous,

40
00:01:26.283 --> 00:01:26.702
memory-safe,

41
00:01:26.702 --> 00:01:27.957
and truly sovereign.

